# tokens
LineComment   "// for is the iteration control statement: it visits every element of a foldable"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// collection in fold order, binding a loop variable to each in turn and running"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// the body once per element. \"of\" binds the value (a list element, a map value);"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// \"in\" binds the key (a map key, a list index) — the JS reading. The loop"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// variable is an immutable per-iteration binding; accumulation goes through a"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// let (E-15) the body reassigns, so a for that sums or joins folds to a constant"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// exactly as the equivalent fold does. for is a statement: it yields no value."
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// Iterability is foldable (E-16) — a for runs over anything that impls it."
Newline       "\n"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// for over a list with \"of\" sums its elements: the let total is the accumulator"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// the body reassigns each iteration, and the function folds to the total. This"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// is the headline accumulation pattern — the same result fold gives, written as"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// a loop for readability."
Newline       "\n"
